# BioVault — what never enters this (public) repository.
# Model weights, signing keys, secrets, app data, and anything exported from your vault
# (docs/09-testing-and-release.md § Repository hygiene; D63, D75).

# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Signing keys ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Android release keystore lives OUTSIDE the repo, with an offline backup (F25).
# These patterns are only a safety net. keystore.properties holds the key password.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties
key.properties
*.pfx
*.p12

# ── Model weights ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fetched or exported locally and verified by checksum, never committed (models/README.md).
/models/*
!/models/README.md
!/models/fetch.*
!/models/SHA256SUMS
*.onnx
*.ort
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.gguf

# ── Your vault data, exports and training data ────────────────────────────
# They reveal what you read and how you connect it. Keep them out of a public repo.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
/exports/
/ml/data/
/ml/artifacts/
*.parquet
links.csv
suggestion_events.csv

# ── Rust ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
target/
**/*.rs.bk

# ── Tauri ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# gen/android is committed (you edit its Gradle files); its build outputs are
# covered by the .gitignore that `tauri android init` writes there.
/app/src-tauri/gen/schemas/
*.apk
*.aab
*.msi
*-setup.exe

# ── Node / front end ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
/app/dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*

# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ── Operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.log
